<BaseLayout title="Engine Selection" description="Choosing an LS engine for a Hyundai Genesis Coupe swap.">
  <h1>Engine Selection</h1>
  <p>
    Almost any Gen III/IV LS will fit with the right mounts and oil pan. The most common choices in the Gen Coupe community are 5.3s, LS1s, and LS3-style engines.
  </p>

  <h2>Common Choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>5.3L (LM7, LY5, etc.)</strong> — cheapest and most available. Plenty of power for a street car; responds well to a cam and headers.</li>
    <li><strong>6.0L (LQ4/LQ9)</strong> — strong iron-block option, good for boost later.</li>
    <li><strong>LS1 / LS2 / LS3</strong> — aluminum, lighter, more aftermarket support. LS3-style is the sweet spot for many Gen Coupe builds.</li>
    <li><strong>LSA / LS9</strong> — supercharged from the factory; more expensive but turn-key power.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Whatever you choose, buy the long-block with accessories if possible (alternator, power steering pump, intake, coils).
    Corvette accessory spacing is often preferred on BK1 for radiator clearance; BK2 has roughly 1.5&quot; more room.
  </p>

